<odoo>
    <!-- Plain <data>, not noupdate="1" like the rest of data/, and on purpose.
         It matches the upstream precedent this record copies,
         addons/sale_timesheet/data/sale_service_data.xml:14-17, which also
         writes this implication outside a noupdate block. With noupdate="1" the
         node would be skipped on every -u (odoo/tools/convert.py:360), so the
         implication would hold only as of install. Without it, each upgrade
         re-applies (4, uom.group_uom): additive and idempotent, and it leaves
         any other implied group alone. The cost, accepted: an administrator
         who removes the implication by hand gets it back on the pack's next
         upgrade, which is the pack insisting its units stay visible, the
         reason the record exists (below). -->
    <data>
        <!-- Every unit field on a bill of material is behind uom.group_uom:
             addons/mrp/views/mrp_bom_views.xml:65 on the form and :102 on the
             component list. That group is granted to nobody by default
             (addons/uom/security/uom_security.xml:4 declares it with no
             implied_ids and no users), and sale_timesheet is the only module in
             the tree that implies it.

             This pack cannot leave it ungranted. Its components are measured in
             grams against raw materials stocked in kilograms, which is the
             whole point of hooks.py's line_uom. Without the group the croissant
             recipe renders "Flour T55 55" with the unit column hidden, beside a
             product the same screen says is stocked in kg. That reads as 55 kg
             of flour in a croissant. The thousandfold misreading the gram lines
             were chosen to prevent then comes back on the screen instead of in
             the data, which is worse: the data is right, so no test can see it.

             Granting it to base.group_user follows the one existing precedent,
             addons/sale_timesheet/data/sale_service_data.xml:15-17. Writing to
             another module's group is what that idiom does; note it is not
             undone by uninstalling this pack. -->
        <record id="base.group_user" model="res.groups">
            <field name="implied_ids" eval="[(4, ref('uom.group_uom'))]"/>
        </record>
    </data>
</odoo>
